  "implementation": [
    "Add GroupFrameOrigin=BoundingBoxCenter/ObjectFrameAverage to command options, script parsing, arguments, remembered preferences, interactive toggles and usage. Keep BoundingBoxCenter as the default; placement mode applies with Rigid and RigidGroups enabled.",
    "Share selected-group origin calculation across object staging and all morph previews. BoundingBoxCenter unions member tight bounds; ObjectFrameAverage averages their individual tight-box centers before evaluating the existing rigid point map. Each selected object or grip owner contributes once; ungrouped objects use their individual tight bounds.",
    "Use the existing FiniteSum mean to avoid intermediate overflow, loss of subnormal coordinates, and accumulation-order changes. Source bounds continue to use the existing geometry kernels and the caller's placement tolerance.",
    "Include the origin mode in the surface preview key and clear cached centers on mode changes. Preserve curve Flow's default placement policy, shared grip precedence, copies, groups, selection and single Undo/Redo behavior.",
    "Extend authored public oracle recipes with bounded multiple-peer fixtures and explicit frame controls. Native diagnostic frames and bounds are expectations only. Compare complete owner records bijectively so copy enumeration order does not affect the result; retain the previous four refit exceptions without widening their bounds."
  ],
  "inferred_native_rule": {
    "group_frame_average": "Arithmetic mean of individual tight-box centers, followed by the existing rigid point map at that origin.",
    "custom_frame_controls": "Public SetObjectFrame/ObjectFrame queries confirm distinct stored custom origins. These edits do not change the captured command placements. Public object frames can also have loose-box origins that differ from the tight centers used by this command.",
    "diagnostics_are_expectations_only": true
  },
